Wait—the question asks WHO JUST HELPED KATRINA PUT THE FLOWERS ON THE TABLE?

Looking closely:  
At [DAY1 11:34:30–11:34:59], Katrina carries the box → puts it on the table → pulls it forward → opens it —all alone per description. No mention of anyone assisting physically until later lines where **Shure** appears nearby (“Shure approached me”), yet even so, they’re seen swinging/standing near; nowhere stated that either person helps move or set down the actual floral arrangement itself into final placement.

But wait! At 11:35:28 – 11:35:30: 
“I’m standing… seeing Shure sway…” Then immediately afterward,
“Seeing Shure approaching.” This suggests interaction may occur shortly thereafter…

However, crucial detail comes much closer together: After opening the package,

> “Alice: Are these peonies?” followed quickly by  

> “Katrinas response,” etc., suggesting dialogue between characters post-opening—not physical aid.

Nowhere explicitly states another character assists in setting the vase/planting/etc.—but note phrase used early: 

> “Put the box straight.”

Then soon after: “So I thought of buying these flowers…”

And finally: “Directly shipped by SF Express, flowers from Yunnan”

No indication ANYONE ELSE moved items INTO PLACE besides Katrina doing everything solo—from carrying to positioning—and thus if asked ‘who helped’, likely implies minimal external input unless implied otherwise...

Yet look more precisely now—at beginning—

She said: “Because I saw … I turned around ...That fits earth day theme."

Later adds: “It wouldnt sprout in seven days”—so clearly planning ahead.

Eventually concludes: “Just right”, meaning timing works fine once placed.

Still though—we see NO ONE actively participating IN PLACEMENT OF FLORAL ARRANGEMENT EXCEPT HERSELF!

Therefore perhaps option c—"ME"—refers to first-person observer narrating events—who could potentially mean THEY were present throughout AND MAY HAVE HELPED UNSTATEDLY BUT NOT DESCRIBED AS SUCH?!

Ah-ha—that makes sense because narrative voice uses 'i' frequently across segments such as:

"I stood," "I continued watching", "I walked toward...", implying speaker observes entire scene—including possible unseen support role behind scenes despite lack of textual confirmation.

Thus although nobody visibly lifts boxes nor places vases beside tables according to text descriptions above—all participants merely watch/listen/react verbally rather than act hands-on regarding setup phase—which means whoever did contribute wasn’t recorded visually OR audibly via speech content within transcript excerpts presented herein.

Hence conclusion remains uncertain due to absence of concrete data point identifying specific helper among listed options—a fact which leads logically towards selecting least incorrect possibility under constraints imposed upon available information sources.

